1
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:07,354
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,354 --> 00:00:08,777
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:37,421 --> 00:00:39,587
Sit. Here.

4
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:41,154
(Episode 20)

5
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:45,054
Drink.

6
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:58,634
Cleaned up, you're really handsome.

7
00:01:00,454 --> 00:01:03,187
Ever thought about becoming an actor?

8
00:01:07,521 --> 00:01:09,046
It's been two weeks, hasn't it?

9
00:01:10,421 --> 00:01:11,610
How have you been?

10
00:01:14,254 --> 00:01:19,420
For the record,
a certain someone keeps dumping me,

11
00:01:19,987 --> 00:01:24,321
so it stings a little, but I'm fine.

12
00:01:31,054 --> 00:01:35,621
At 11 this morning,
I faced Son Ji Yeol at the police station.

13
00:01:37,496 --> 00:01:38,587
I see.

14
00:01:41,187 --> 00:01:44,154
He said he was sorry,
that he deserved to die.

15
00:01:45,587 --> 00:01:49,287
That if I spared him just once,
he'd spend his life making up for it.

16
00:01:50,954 --> 00:01:52,887
He begged me on his knees, crying.

17
00:01:53,221 --> 00:01:56,821
So? Are you going to spare him?

18
00:02:04,487 --> 00:02:06,121
I'm going to forgive myself first.

19
00:02:08,154 --> 00:02:11,902
I'll forgive myself first, and once I can,

20
00:02:12,902 --> 00:02:15,162
I'll think about that bastard then.

21
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:21,441
I slept the whole two weeks.

22
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:25,179
Because I couldn't stand
the sight of myself.

23
00:02:27,954 --> 00:02:32,087
I couldn't stand the sound of me
breathing, talking, walking around,

24
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:37,621
or any sound that proved I was alive,

25
00:02:38,822 --> 00:02:40,668
so I just kept sleeping.

26
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,013
Right.

27
00:02:45,087 --> 00:02:46,753
I went through that too.

28
00:02:48,587 --> 00:02:52,636
I was so pathetic,
so annoyed and fed up with myself,

29
00:02:52,886 --> 00:02:59,150
that I spent a whole month lying around,
not moving, just sleeping...

30
00:03:01,936 --> 00:03:03,609
I've been there too.

31
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:11,928
So, are you done sleeping?

32
00:03:13,621 --> 00:03:15,587
If you've slept enough, get up now.

33
00:03:18,587 --> 00:03:23,384
Get up, brush your teeth,
wash your face, eat something,

34
00:03:24,021 --> 00:03:26,954
have some coffee, get some sun,

35
00:03:27,587 --> 00:03:32,321
and take a quick look at the sky like this
to see if the earth is still spinning.

36
00:03:34,787 --> 00:03:40,354
Once you've done all that
and there's nothing left to do,

37
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:44,326
when you're so bored you could die,

38
00:03:45,046 --> 00:03:46,319
couldn't you forgive yourself then?

39
00:03:47,454 --> 00:03:52,287
And personally, Son Ji Yeol...

40
00:03:53,154 --> 00:03:56,487
I recommend you don't forgive
that bunch of villains.

41
00:04:03,754 --> 00:04:04,920
Do you like pasta?

42
00:04:06,521 --> 00:04:10,087
I got some killer truffles in last night,

43
00:04:10,263 --> 00:04:12,354
so let's grate a ton over some pasta.

44
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:15,476
I'm not trying to take credit.
No, actually, I am.

45
00:04:16,854 --> 00:04:19,921
You at least know
how precious truffles are, right?

46
00:04:21,739 --> 00:04:23,454
Looks like you have no idea...

47
00:04:25,501 --> 00:04:29,687
My roommate is the co-owner
and manager here.

48
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:33,768
If he picks a fight or glares at you,
just ignore him.

49
00:04:33,901 --> 00:04:37,698
He's tall, but he's as petty as they come.

50
00:04:37,723 --> 00:04:39,944
He's a good guy, though.

51
00:04:40,744 --> 00:04:41,851
Get some rest.

52
00:05:12,852 --> 00:05:14,421
What is it, Mom?

53
00:05:15,921 --> 00:05:19,021
Looks like Gyu O is looking up at the sky.

54
00:05:20,421 --> 00:05:22,387
He's looking at the sky, Gyu O is.

55
00:05:22,474 --> 00:05:24,600
I look at the sky too, Mom.

56
00:05:24,754 --> 00:05:28,196
I looked at it at school
and this morning too.

57
00:05:28,435 --> 00:05:30,275
I look at it every day.

58
00:05:30,321 --> 00:05:35,221
Exactly. You look at the sky every day,

59
00:05:35,521 --> 00:05:39,503
but it seemed like Gyu O didn't,
and that worried me.

60
00:05:39,773 --> 00:05:42,106
But ta-da, look at this.

61
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:45,740
Gyu O sent me a picture of the sky.

62
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:48,229
I'm so happy.

63
00:05:48,254 --> 00:05:52,287
I can take a picture
of the sky and send it too.

64
00:05:52,354 --> 00:05:55,721
Of course. You can do anything.

65
00:05:55,954 --> 00:06:00,054
A multitasker. No,
you're good at everything, my boy.

66
00:06:03,387 --> 00:06:09,421
But Mom, I think Gyu O
is a frog in hibernation. Right?

67
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:14,392
He's asleep when I go to school
and when I come home.

68
00:06:14,825 --> 00:06:16,981
He's always sleeping. Right?

69
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:22,604
No, Gyeol.
I think Gyu O is done sleeping now.

70
00:06:23,054 --> 00:06:28,854
Looks like Gyu O is finally up and awake.

71
00:06:33,621 --> 00:06:35,700
I get up too, Mom.

72
00:06:35,914 --> 00:06:38,847
I got up this morning too.

73
00:06:47,921 --> 00:06:51,462
I'll be wearing pink.
You'll spot me right away.

74
00:07:01,721 --> 00:07:03,087
Is that my brother, by any chance?

75
00:07:04,721 --> 00:07:06,354
That napkin is Han Gyu O, isn't it?

76
00:07:12,587 --> 00:07:14,103
What did you just say?

77
00:07:14,921 --> 00:07:17,665
Give up on my brother, Ms. Kwon.

78
00:07:18,561 --> 00:07:20,555
Didn't you tell me not to give up?

79
00:07:20,882 --> 00:07:23,349
You told me not to give up
and to set him straight.

80
00:07:23,987 --> 00:07:26,081
Back then,
I said that because he's my brother...

81
00:07:26,921 --> 00:07:30,573
I don't care about anyone else's life.
My family comes first.

82
00:07:31,813 --> 00:07:33,366
But all he does is sleep.

83
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:37,647
Anyway, he's not even trying to change,
and you're way too good for him.

84
00:07:38,854 --> 00:07:40,257
I wasn't thinking.

85
00:07:41,366 --> 00:07:42,952
So he's not your brother now?

86
00:07:43,357 --> 00:07:46,544
Did your father disown Gyu O or something?

87
00:07:46,954 --> 00:07:49,387
He'll always be my brother
until the day I die,

88
00:07:49,862 --> 00:07:52,729
but for you, cutting ties with someone
like him as soon as possible...

89
00:07:52,754 --> 00:07:54,854
is the shortcut to a longer life.

90
00:07:54,954 --> 00:07:56,821
What are you talking about?

91
00:07:56,846 --> 00:07:59,499
My brother ignores
your calls and your texts,

92
00:07:59,524 --> 00:08:01,753
ticks you off, makes you angry,
and leaves you hanging.

93
00:08:02,354 --> 00:08:04,594
He's got you stressed out like crazy.

94
00:08:05,487 --> 00:08:09,916
He keeps you from sleeping, from eating,
and has you shredding napkins.

95
00:08:10,635 --> 00:08:13,113
He's a total troublemaker,
so why date someone like that?

96
00:08:14,254 --> 00:08:16,038
Who said I wanted a longer life?

97
00:08:16,271 --> 00:08:17,985
Who asked you for a shortcut?

98
00:08:19,507 --> 00:08:21,862
I'm parched. Can I drink this?

99
00:08:35,687 --> 00:08:38,854
Are you jealous of your brother,
by any chance?

100
00:08:39,721 --> 00:08:43,454
Worried he'll hit it off
with a great, pretty woman like me?

101
00:08:43,694 --> 00:08:45,890
I could die for my brother.

102
00:08:46,414 --> 00:08:47,896
If my brother were drowning,

103
00:08:47,921 --> 00:08:49,784
and I might die trying to save him,

104
00:08:50,021 --> 00:08:55,336
would I still jump in?
Yes. I'd just jump in.

105
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,289
So you don't trust me.

106
00:09:10,295 --> 00:09:12,055
You're afraid I'll hurt him.

107
00:09:13,026 --> 00:09:16,660
Worried I'll break his heart. That's it.

108
00:09:17,321 --> 00:09:19,485
You're afraid I'll really give up on him,

109
00:09:20,546 --> 00:09:22,699
so you're beating me to it.

110
00:09:23,654 --> 00:09:25,108
That's not it.

111
00:09:25,641 --> 00:09:28,596
It's not. It's really not.

112
00:09:28,621 --> 00:09:31,621
Don't lie. You're not even good at it.

113
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,787
Now I have one more reason
not to give up on Han Gyu O.

114
00:09:39,354 --> 00:09:44,021
Why would I give up on Han Gyu O
when you're such a sweet brother?

115
00:09:45,821 --> 00:09:48,921
I really want to marry Han Gyu O
and become part of your family.

116
00:09:50,514 --> 00:09:52,158
I'm going to make it happen.

117
00:10:00,321 --> 00:10:02,636
The night sky is so pretty too, Gyu O.

118
00:10:02,967 --> 00:10:06,762
They say you can see stars somewhere
with clean air or at an observatory.

119
00:10:06,787 --> 00:10:09,087
Let's go see them together someday.

120
00:10:10,721 --> 00:10:14,421
(Su Nam)

121
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,466
Yes, Su Nam.

122
00:10:16,854 --> 00:10:18,687
I just finished the delivery
and I'm on my way.

123
00:10:19,287 --> 00:10:21,387
I'm almost there. I'm close by.

124
00:10:21,721 --> 00:10:22,854
Okay.

125
00:10:35,314 --> 00:10:39,672
Gyu Rim is almost here,
so wait just a bit.

126
00:10:40,721 --> 00:10:46,604
From now on, Gyu Rim
will be in charge of this place.

127
00:10:47,243 --> 00:10:48,560
Are you going somewhere, ma'am?

128
00:10:49,459 --> 00:10:52,372
Well, it's not like I'm going far.

129
00:10:53,853 --> 00:10:59,603
But ever since you walked in,
you've looked awfully familiar.

130
00:11:00,454 --> 00:11:03,487
- Me?
- Yes, hold on.

131
00:11:03,487 --> 00:11:06,787
Why do you look so familiar?

132
00:11:06,887 --> 00:11:10,973
I've definitely seen you somewhere,
but where?

133
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:21,867
What's going on with people lately?

134
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:25,421
I guess I really do have a common face.

135
00:11:25,421 --> 00:11:28,087
Even on my way here,
someone asked if they knew me...

136
00:11:28,087 --> 00:11:30,887
If that face is common,

137
00:11:30,887 --> 00:11:33,002
then pigs can fly.

138
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:36,676
Look me straight in the eye.

139
00:11:36,921 --> 00:11:39,893
I'll figure it out somehow.

140
00:11:43,547 --> 00:11:45,267
My goodness, I've got it.

141
00:11:45,753 --> 00:11:47,353
I know who you are.

142
00:11:51,621 --> 00:11:53,654
Just kidding.

143
00:11:54,447 --> 00:11:57,442
Where would I have seen
a famous restaurant chef?

144
00:12:00,921 --> 00:12:04,254
My tongue is failing me,
and my eyesight is going too.

145
00:12:05,054 --> 00:12:06,887
I'm all washed up now.

146
00:12:07,054 --> 00:12:10,331
I've turned into useless junk.

147
00:12:11,187 --> 00:12:12,554
I'm back.

148
00:12:13,799 --> 00:12:15,914
Say hello.

149
00:12:15,939 --> 00:12:18,606
He's a famous restaurant chef.

150
00:12:19,313 --> 00:12:24,013
He wants our shop to supply him
with radish water kimchi and white kimchi,

151
00:12:24,054 --> 00:12:27,113
and he says he'll pay
whatever price we name.

152
00:12:27,233 --> 00:12:29,764
I'll come pick up
the kimchi myself every day.

153
00:12:29,854 --> 00:12:32,127
You'll come in person, Chef?

154
00:12:32,207 --> 00:12:38,358
He means he'll taste it himself
every day before he buys it.

155
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:41,478
Sharp as a tack.

156
00:12:44,606 --> 00:12:45,721
Su Nam.

157
00:12:45,954 --> 00:12:48,754
We're short on radish water kimchi
and white kimchi for the store as it is.

158
00:12:49,087 --> 00:12:50,829
We can't handle supplying him too.

159
00:12:51,121 --> 00:12:53,691
I already signed the contract.

160
00:12:53,716 --> 00:12:56,901
It's a done deal, so make it work somehow.

161
00:12:58,213 --> 00:13:00,256
Then I'll see you tomorrow morning.

162
00:13:01,221 --> 00:13:06,621
Sorry about earlier,
saying you looked familiar and all.

163
00:13:06,646 --> 00:13:07,954
Not at all.

164
00:13:07,979 --> 00:13:09,399
- Take care now.
- I will.

165
00:13:13,454 --> 00:13:16,909
I'll get to see
that handsome face every day.

166
00:13:19,854 --> 00:13:23,032
If I had a daughter,
I'd grab him for a son-in-law.

167
00:13:23,214 --> 00:13:27,389
Handsome, capable, smart, meticulous.

168
00:13:28,173 --> 00:13:31,510
And he's a chef,
so he must be a good cook too.

169
00:13:33,713 --> 00:13:37,459
If you were going to dump my son,
it should've been for a man like that.

170
00:13:37,513 --> 00:13:41,583
If you dumped my son
and went to a man like that,

171
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:44,146
I'd be okay with it.

172
00:13:44,171 --> 00:13:46,143
I'd accept it.

173
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,954
He's too good to give away.

174
00:13:50,321 --> 00:13:53,721
Since things with my son
are hopeless anyway,

175
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:58,767
should I just say you're my daughter
and set you up with him?

176
00:13:59,254 --> 00:14:00,254
Su Nam.

177
00:14:01,454 --> 00:14:03,454
I know. That's going too far.

178
00:14:05,367 --> 00:14:07,067
I should've had one more daughter.

179
00:14:07,581 --> 00:14:13,204
What was so urgent that my husband
had to go before me?

180
00:14:13,421 --> 00:14:14,887
Honestly...

181
00:14:51,681 --> 00:14:53,114
(AI Voice. Please speak.)

182
00:14:53,139 --> 00:14:55,439
There's someone I like,

183
00:14:56,068 --> 00:14:59,668
but he and I can never be together.

184
00:15:02,087 --> 00:15:04,021
But he won't give up.

185
00:15:06,007 --> 00:15:10,007
No matter how hard I push him away,
he doesn't listen.

186
00:15:10,853 --> 00:15:15,087
Can you tell me how to make him
so disappointed and sick of me...

187
00:15:16,047 --> 00:15:19,841
that he runs away from me?

188
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:24,633
The hardest part isn't knowing
how to end it firmly,

189
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:27,752
it's never leaving any room for hope.

190
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,380
People cling to possibilities
more than words.

191
00:15:32,199 --> 00:15:37,442
But think carefully about whether you want
to end this for the other person's sake,

192
00:15:37,587 --> 00:15:43,378
or because you're afraid of a future
where you'll let him down someday.

193
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:46,900
If it's the latter,
how can I make him run...

194
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,301
It's not a dream, Mu Jin.

195
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,300
It's really me, Gyu Rim.

196
00:16:14,374 --> 00:16:17,207
I thought if I came around now,
I could catch you.

197
00:16:19,174 --> 00:16:21,308
If you showed up out of nowhere
this early,

198
00:16:22,301 --> 00:16:24,134
it can't be good news, can it?

199
00:16:26,266 --> 00:16:29,795
Just 30 minutes before I woke up,
I was having a really happy dream.

200
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,733
A dream where we went back
to nine years ago.

201
00:16:33,321 --> 00:16:35,287
Like we were the only two people
in the world,

202
00:16:35,687 --> 00:16:40,021
like we'd never break up,
loving each other like crazy.

203
00:16:40,687 --> 00:16:44,254
So if you're going to say something harsh,
like telling me to get lost,

204
00:16:44,587 --> 00:16:47,254
save it for next time.

205
00:16:47,787 --> 00:16:49,421
I really want to be happy today.

206
00:16:49,851 --> 00:16:51,487
I had such an amazing dream.

207
00:16:51,577 --> 00:16:55,454
All right. Let's do what you said.

208
00:16:57,348 --> 00:17:00,448
Let's see this through
and find out where we end up.

209
00:17:03,054 --> 00:17:05,254
Let's get back together.

210
00:17:08,521 --> 00:17:10,687
Like nine years ago.

211
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:13,307
As if we'd never broken up.

212
00:17:31,497 --> 00:17:34,117
What? Is there a problem
with the report you turned in?

213
00:17:34,291 --> 00:17:37,476
The report is perfect. I'm Han Gyu Yeong.

214
00:17:37,501 --> 00:17:40,317
Then why do you look like
you're about to tear your hair out?

215
00:17:46,126 --> 00:17:50,431
I think I got tricked into this marriage,
Se Hui.

216
00:17:53,313 --> 00:17:56,447
Weren't you the one doing the tricking?

217
00:17:59,757 --> 00:18:01,738
You're the one who pulled the con.

218
00:18:01,896 --> 00:18:04,092
Calling Chairman Jang your father.

219
00:18:04,929 --> 00:18:07,403
Why didn't I cut you off sooner?

220
00:18:09,398 --> 00:18:13,041
Because if you cut me off too,
you'd have no friends left?

221
00:18:27,789 --> 00:18:30,196
What? What now?

222
00:18:36,118 --> 00:18:37,126
(Honey)

223
00:18:40,656 --> 00:18:41,656
Where are you?

224
00:18:43,319 --> 00:18:44,770
Meet me at home in an hour.

225
00:18:46,277 --> 00:18:48,929
I'm taking a half day,
so you take one too.

226
00:18:51,270 --> 00:18:55,409
Turns out Cho Heung Sik
really is a distant cousin of mine.

227
00:18:55,434 --> 00:18:57,486
I just got a very interesting photo.

228
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,637
Should I take it to Cho Heung Sik, then?

229
00:18:59,887 --> 00:19:01,447
Take a half day, I said!

230
00:19:06,024 --> 00:19:08,502
I should send this to Jeong Mi.

231
00:19:13,283 --> 00:19:14,544
What are you doing?

232
00:19:17,064 --> 00:19:18,957
Distant cousin, my foot.

233
00:19:19,097 --> 00:19:20,627
What's going on between
you and Cho Heung Sik?

234
00:19:20,928 --> 00:19:22,950
Are you two having an affair? An affair?

235
00:19:23,103 --> 00:19:24,147
What?

236
00:19:24,253 --> 00:19:25,469
Affair? Give me a break.

237
00:19:25,494 --> 00:19:27,196
You think I'm like you?

238
00:19:28,203 --> 00:19:30,745
Hey, you, I swear!

239
00:19:31,131 --> 00:19:32,376
Go ahead, hit me.

240
00:19:32,378 --> 00:19:36,215
If I tell him, this time you'll need
full upper and lower dentures.

241
00:19:46,370 --> 00:19:47,979
This was taken a long time ago.

242
00:19:48,004 --> 00:19:49,895
Way before I married you.

243
00:19:51,164 --> 00:19:53,665
You think I won my Ph.D. in a card game?

244
00:19:53,784 --> 00:19:54,784
What?

245
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,055
You think I'm an idiot?

246
00:19:57,057 --> 00:19:58,728
That's the outfit I bought you a week ago.

247
00:19:58,730 --> 00:20:00,084
The one you're wearing in the photo.

248
00:20:00,085 --> 00:20:01,701
You filthy jerk.

249
00:20:01,726 --> 00:20:04,005
Filthy!

250
00:20:04,884 --> 00:20:06,485
What are you doing?

251
00:20:06,523 --> 00:20:08,132
Mom.

252
00:20:09,909 --> 00:20:12,757
What kind of behavior
is this for a new bride?

253
00:20:13,811 --> 00:20:17,704
You two should be lovebirds,
so why are you hitting him?

254
00:20:18,757 --> 00:20:20,710
It seems he is still seeing that woman.

255
00:20:20,711 --> 00:20:22,511
He's busy being a lovebird with her.

256
00:20:22,536 --> 00:20:23,536
What?

257
00:20:23,657 --> 00:20:26,542
Hey,
you still haven't gotten rid of that girl?

258
00:20:26,567 --> 00:20:28,597
What can I do if she won't let go?

259
00:20:28,599 --> 00:20:31,646
She says she'll die if I leave her.
What am I supposed to do?

260
00:20:32,487 --> 00:20:35,766
- I'm going crazy too. This is hard on me.
- Like father, like son...

261
00:20:35,951 --> 00:20:38,384
Of all things, you had to take after that?

262
00:20:38,385 --> 00:20:40,431
Of all things to learn,
you had to learn that?

263
00:20:41,504 --> 00:20:46,466
How did your father raise you?

264
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:49,317
Worry about your own life, Mom.

265
00:20:49,318 --> 00:20:50,931
Stop seeing those host bar boys!

266
00:20:51,164 --> 00:20:52,972
Hey! You little...

267
00:20:53,498 --> 00:20:56,853
- What are you talking about?
- Don't play dumb.

268
00:20:56,970 --> 00:21:00,073
Everyone in Gangnam knows
you go to host bars.

269
00:21:01,124 --> 00:21:03,723
Do you like guys young enough
to be your sons that much?

270
00:21:04,077 --> 00:21:05,755
Why, you little...!

271
00:21:05,881 --> 00:21:07,904
- Hey.
- What?

272
00:21:07,905 --> 00:21:09,498
Be quiet, will you? Shut your mouth.

273
00:21:44,777 --> 00:21:46,867
Should I work part-time here with you too?

274
00:21:50,950 --> 00:21:51,950
You're crazy.

275
00:21:52,313 --> 00:21:53,844
Are we the kind of friends
who work part-time together?

276
00:21:54,306 --> 00:21:55,957
What, we can't even
work part-time together?

277
00:21:57,377 --> 00:21:59,603
I told you there's nothing
between Seo Min Ju and me,

278
00:21:59,710 --> 00:22:00,964
and there never will be.

279
00:22:01,784 --> 00:22:03,109
As for upsetting you,

280
00:22:04,170 --> 00:22:06,737
didn't the beating
I took back then settle that?

281
00:22:07,742 --> 00:22:09,389
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

282
00:22:09,958 --> 00:22:13,313
Here's your meat. Enjoy.

283
00:22:36,149 --> 00:22:43,149
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae)

284
00:22:46,588 --> 00:22:48,341
(Wife)

285
00:22:49,024 --> 00:22:50,497
Are you doing okay?

286
00:22:57,537 --> 00:22:58,930
You're not sick?

287
00:22:59,631 --> 00:23:01,918
You're eating properly, right?

288
00:23:08,643 --> 00:23:09,643
Yes.

289
00:23:11,851 --> 00:23:14,022
I'm doing well.

290
00:23:15,353 --> 00:23:16,707
How about you?

291
00:23:18,123 --> 00:23:20,460
Is the housekeeper feeding you well?

292
00:23:22,247 --> 00:23:27,047
She knows all your tastes,
so I'm not worried, though.

293
00:23:27,963 --> 00:23:30,384
No need to worry.
I'm eating well. Of course.

294
00:23:31,104 --> 00:23:33,303
I'm doing fine, so don't worry.

295
00:23:34,597 --> 00:23:36,706
Thank you. I'm glad you're doing well.

296
00:23:41,389 --> 00:23:46,612
Can I ask where you're staying
and what you're up to?

297
00:23:49,904 --> 00:23:54,052
I started working part-time
at a barbecue restaurant.

298
00:23:54,363 --> 00:23:55,993
The place I'm staying is nearby too.

299
00:23:57,811 --> 00:24:00,614
A barbecue restaurant?

300
00:24:01,442 --> 00:24:04,671
I hear even young people find
that kind of work hard...

301
00:24:06,423 --> 00:24:08,731
If it weren't hard, would it be work?

302
00:24:09,948 --> 00:24:11,227
It's fun.

303
00:24:12,231 --> 00:24:16,608
I'm working hard physically,
so I sleep well and food tastes great.

304
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:18,834
I see. That's a relief.

305
00:24:19,493 --> 00:24:21,354
Is the food good there?

306
00:24:21,699 --> 00:24:23,491
Could I come eat there sometime?

307
00:24:27,764 --> 00:24:29,886
Yes. It's good.

308
00:24:30,094 --> 00:24:31,500
Come by sometime.

309
00:24:31,757 --> 00:24:32,757
Excuse me.

310
00:24:33,304 --> 00:24:35,139
Yes, just a moment.

311
00:24:35,853 --> 00:24:37,661
I'll call you back later.

312
00:24:39,783 --> 00:24:41,283
Yes, coming.

313
00:24:49,270 --> 00:24:52,320
You're not really thinking
of leaving me, are you?

314
00:24:56,097 --> 00:24:57,774
That's not it, is it?

315
00:25:16,482 --> 00:25:18,629
(Kim Gyu Seo)

316
00:25:20,637 --> 00:25:23,177
- Hello?
- Hello, this is Kim Gyu Seo.

317
00:25:23,417 --> 00:25:25,865
We met near the shopping arcade
in Geumje Dong...

318
00:25:26,283 --> 00:25:28,073
Yes, I remember.

319
00:25:28,153 --> 00:25:30,540
- How have you been?
- Good.

320
00:25:31,419 --> 00:25:33,434
You said you'd buy me a meal,

321
00:25:33,802 --> 00:25:35,550
and that I could call anytime...

322
00:25:36,330 --> 00:25:38,371
I'm totally free this evening.

323
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:43,790
Then I'll see you this evening.

324
00:25:44,267 --> 00:25:46,577
I'll text you the place.

325
00:25:47,383 --> 00:25:48,750
Okay, thank you.

326
00:25:50,604 --> 00:25:52,544
Why are you meeting Gyu Rim's mom?

327
00:25:52,950 --> 00:25:54,959
And lying about your name, too?

328
00:25:55,030 --> 00:25:57,866
- I'm curious.
- About what?

329
00:25:57,891 --> 00:26:00,602
Whether she met a man
100 times better than our dad,

330
00:26:00,604 --> 00:26:02,851
and is living a happy life.

331
00:26:02,918 --> 00:26:05,590
Is there any man in the world
worse than our dad?

332
00:26:05,615 --> 00:26:08,628
And if she isn't happy,
what are you going to do about it?

333
00:26:08,653 --> 00:26:10,121
Set her up on a blind date?

334
00:26:10,228 --> 00:26:11,337
What are you, Mr. Responsibility?

335
00:26:11,730 --> 00:26:14,758
You try to take responsibility
for everything in the world.

336
00:26:16,368 --> 00:26:17,689
Did you give up on your diet?

337
00:26:19,457 --> 00:26:22,090
Why would I give up? It's because of you.

338
00:26:22,115 --> 00:26:23,909
The kids keep trying
to get on your good side,

339
00:26:23,934 --> 00:26:26,160
so they keep pushing bread on me.

340
00:26:26,190 --> 00:26:28,104
If I can't lose weight,
it's your fault, Han Gyu Seo.

341
00:26:42,595 --> 00:26:44,017
What are you doing here?

342
00:26:44,243 --> 00:26:45,732
Shouldn't you be at work?

343
00:26:46,056 --> 00:26:49,869
I went in yesterday morning and worked
straight through until just now.

344
00:26:50,481 --> 00:26:52,096
Didn't get a wink of sleep.

345
00:26:52,230 --> 00:26:53,756
Then go home and sleep.

346
00:26:53,910 --> 00:26:56,177
This is the rooftop
of Mu Jin's restaurant.

347
00:26:56,229 --> 00:26:59,720
What if you run into Mu Jin?

348
00:27:01,437 --> 00:27:03,032
If I run into him, I run into him.

349
00:27:03,437 --> 00:27:04,689
Did I commit a crime?

350
00:27:05,116 --> 00:27:07,606
What are we, sworn enemies?

351
00:27:09,497 --> 00:27:10,651
Right, you're right.

352
00:27:10,849 --> 00:27:13,664
It's not like you two are enemies
for life,

353
00:27:15,651 --> 00:27:17,337
or like you'll never see each other again.

354
00:27:19,144 --> 00:27:22,011
Seo Hyeon.

355
00:27:23,861 --> 00:27:25,610
Since when did you get so thoughtful?

356
00:27:28,157 --> 00:27:31,050
To you, I'm still Jang Seo Hyeon,
the middle schooler, right?

357
00:27:31,557 --> 00:27:33,089
Of course, middle schooler.

358
00:27:34,926 --> 00:27:37,823
I'm hungry.
I want my mom's soybean paste stew...

359
00:27:39,524 --> 00:27:41,696
I want black bean noodles.

360
00:27:50,564 --> 00:27:53,211
You're the only one I can ask, so...

361
00:27:53,617 --> 00:27:55,076
Sure, go ahead.

362
00:27:57,523 --> 00:28:02,467
If my mom and dad get divorced,
is it because of me?

363
00:28:08,516 --> 00:28:10,766
Are they getting divorced?

364
00:28:11,837 --> 00:28:15,323
If they do, is it because of me?

365
00:28:15,683 --> 00:28:18,356
Am I 100 percent the reason?

366
00:28:23,804 --> 00:28:24,877
Why won't you answer?

367
00:28:25,333 --> 00:28:26,744
I'm asking you.

368
00:28:26,817 --> 00:28:28,591
Mom left home because of me.

369
00:28:28,719 --> 00:28:30,181
If they divorce,
that'll be because of me too.

370
00:28:30,346 --> 00:28:32,167
Is everything my fault?

371
00:28:34,957 --> 00:28:37,394
You never shut up for a second.
Why won't you answer me now?

372
00:28:37,450 --> 00:28:39,621
Say something, Park Jeong Woo!

373
00:29:18,162 --> 00:29:20,809
Did I say banana milk?

374
00:29:22,883 --> 00:29:24,209
I said strawberry milk.

375
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:27,849
Really? I must've heard wrong.

376
00:29:27,851 --> 00:29:29,111
I'll go buy it again.

377
00:29:40,137 --> 00:29:41,847
Did I say strawberry milk?

378
00:29:42,057 --> 00:29:43,924
Didn't I say chocolate milk?

379
00:29:50,271 --> 00:29:51,711
You want chocolate milk.

380
00:29:52,812 --> 00:29:54,423
I'll be right back.

381
00:30:11,709 --> 00:30:13,280
Chocolate milk it is.

382
00:30:15,303 --> 00:30:17,219
Maybe I should just have plain milk.

383
00:30:18,683 --> 00:30:21,442
Maybe because it's so early,
I'm not craving anything sweet.

384
00:30:26,188 --> 00:30:28,824
Right. If you're not craving it,
you shouldn't have it.

385
00:30:29,344 --> 00:30:30,424
You want plain milk, right?

386
00:30:30,469 --> 00:30:31,677
I'll go get plain milk.

387
00:30:45,144 --> 00:30:48,668
Take your pick.
I cleaned out the whole store,

388
00:30:48,702 --> 00:30:50,498
so pick whatever you want to drink.

389
00:30:54,317 --> 00:30:57,088
- Are you trying to stuff me?
- What?

390
00:30:57,245 --> 00:30:59,596
You want me to drink
all this until I burst?

391
00:30:59,770 --> 00:31:01,005
Showing off how rich you are?

392
00:31:01,049 --> 00:31:02,763
What am I, a rhino at a watering hole?

393
00:31:03,208 --> 00:31:04,619
That's not it...

394
00:31:05,881 --> 00:31:07,721
I just brought everything for now,

395
00:31:07,723 --> 00:31:10,383
so you could pick what you want.

396
00:31:12,911 --> 00:31:14,831
How can you make me feel so pathetic?

397
00:31:15,411 --> 00:31:17,734
Is money everything?
Does being rich give you the right...

398
00:31:17,736 --> 00:31:19,377
to trample on people's pride like that?

399
00:31:25,793 --> 00:31:27,450
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

400
00:31:28,598 --> 00:31:31,306
I was wrong. I didn't think it through.

401
00:31:31,357 --> 00:31:34,262
I'm in such a bad mood that I don't want
to say a word right now.

402
00:31:34,811 --> 00:31:36,833
- Gyu Rim.
- I'm leaving.

403
00:31:51,467 --> 00:31:54,644
What was that? What's wrong with her?

404
00:31:56,913 --> 00:31:58,832
She never acts like...

405
00:32:00,725 --> 00:32:03,489
No. I was wrong.

406
00:32:05,377 --> 00:32:07,059
She had every right to be angry.

407
00:32:08,934 --> 00:32:10,454
You're the worst, Han Gyu Rim.

408
00:32:15,712 --> 00:32:17,007
What do I do?

409
00:32:18,698 --> 00:32:19,920
No. That was good.

410
00:32:19,921 --> 00:32:21,906
Good. That's how he'll get sick of me.

411
00:32:21,981 --> 00:32:23,867
That's how he'll lose interest
and run away.

412
00:32:24,126 --> 00:32:25,607
It's fine. You did great.

413
00:32:31,827 --> 00:32:32,827
Excuse me.

414
00:32:33,889 --> 00:32:36,823
Su Nam wants you
to come over for a minute.

415
00:32:39,327 --> 00:32:40,327
Sorry?

416
00:32:45,064 --> 00:32:46,970
(Special Notice, Closed for one week
for interior renovations)

417
00:32:46,972 --> 00:32:48,350
(Up to 50% off all items, special sale)

418
00:32:48,375 --> 00:32:50,261
When did you get all dressed up like this?

419
00:32:54,034 --> 00:32:56,014
You look so pretty, Su Nam.

420
00:32:58,060 --> 00:33:02,504
As of right now, I've got a new job.

421
00:33:02,765 --> 00:33:06,028
From now on, I'm the boss here.

422
00:33:06,321 --> 00:33:10,593
And from now on,
you're the boss of Suragan over there.

423
00:33:11,527 --> 00:33:13,274
What do you mean?

424
00:33:13,299 --> 00:33:16,752
The side dish shop closing
for a week starting tomorrow...

425
00:33:16,966 --> 00:33:19,179
isn't for renovations.

426
00:33:19,453 --> 00:33:23,736
It's to get you ready to be the boss.
Just so you know.

427
00:33:23,761 --> 00:33:25,332
No way.

428
00:33:25,335 --> 00:33:27,896
How could I be the boss?
That's ridiculous, Su Nam.

429
00:33:27,921 --> 00:33:30,226
Then should I hand it over
to a total stranger?

430
00:33:33,221 --> 00:33:36,654
Or to my Heung Sik,
who can't even make ramen?

431
00:33:37,074 --> 00:33:39,884
Do you know how hard I worked
to keep that place going?

432
00:33:40,059 --> 00:33:42,894
Great location, lots of regulars,

433
00:33:43,222 --> 00:33:46,263
it's the best of the best.

434
00:33:48,420 --> 00:33:52,553
If you really can't do it,
I'll just shut it down, period.

435
00:33:53,275 --> 00:33:54,275
Thank you.

436
00:33:55,734 --> 00:33:57,994
You can just keep running it.

437
00:33:58,372 --> 00:34:00,428
You didn't say a word about it
until just now,

438
00:34:00,648 --> 00:34:03,293
and suddenly you're opening
a medical device store?

439
00:34:03,407 --> 00:34:06,100
You know my nephew who ran this place?

440
00:34:06,570 --> 00:34:08,722
He has to go to America,

441
00:34:08,724 --> 00:34:12,107
and he said he couldn't hand over
something this good to a stranger.

442
00:34:13,151 --> 00:34:15,786
"Nephew, great minds think alike."

443
00:34:16,181 --> 00:34:19,493
He and I high-fived, and anyway,

444
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:22,377
that's not the point.

445
00:34:24,015 --> 00:34:25,499
Will you do it or not?

446
00:34:25,840 --> 00:34:29,589
Will you take on that gold mine or not?

447
00:34:31,474 --> 00:34:33,274
Still, I can't, Su Nam.

448
00:34:33,801 --> 00:34:35,807
Who am I to be the boss?

449
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:37,026
I couldn't possibly.

450
00:34:37,734 --> 00:34:40,280
You think I was born a boss?

451
00:34:42,621 --> 00:34:44,121
Guess I can't keep up
the classy act anymore.

452
00:34:48,044 --> 00:34:52,947
At some point, my taste buds quit on me,
and now I can't taste anything.

453
00:34:53,915 --> 00:34:57,427
I can't taste sour,
and I can't taste sweet.

454
00:35:02,034 --> 00:35:04,610
You kind of knew too.

455
00:35:05,446 --> 00:35:07,307
With my taste gone like this,

456
00:35:08,169 --> 00:35:11,138
how can I run a side dish shop?

457
00:35:13,500 --> 00:35:16,437
- Su Nam.
- You really are something.

458
00:35:16,487 --> 00:35:19,820
When someone offers you something,
you just take it gratefully.

459
00:35:20,294 --> 00:35:24,394
Why make me confess my weakness like this?

460
00:35:25,288 --> 00:35:27,866
After all the work it took
to patch things up between us,

461
00:35:27,891 --> 00:35:29,758
do we have to fall out again?

462
00:35:30,867 --> 00:35:36,010
Being too humble and too nice
is exhausting.

463
00:35:36,454 --> 00:35:40,273
Boss boot camp starts tomorrow,
so get your head on straight.

464
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:47,349
How big is the lot here?

465
00:35:48,781 --> 00:35:50,439
Mr. Han.

466
00:35:51,791 --> 00:35:53,985
Hey, what time is it?

467
00:35:53,987 --> 00:35:55,487
When an elder calls,
you come running right away.

468
00:35:55,914 --> 00:35:57,401
You've gotten sloppy.

469
00:35:57,769 --> 00:36:00,154
I'm only two minutes late.

470
00:36:00,561 --> 00:36:03,454
I ran so fast after your call,
I nearly left my shoes behind.

471
00:36:05,045 --> 00:36:08,511
We should've just grilled pork belly.
Italian doesn't suit you.

472
00:36:08,536 --> 00:36:09,711
- Let's go already.
- Hey.

473
00:36:10,787 --> 00:36:13,033
This place belongs to the guy
who likes Gyu Rim.

474
00:36:13,641 --> 00:36:16,115
I mean, they dated and broke up before,

475
00:36:16,157 --> 00:36:18,374
and now he wants another shot.

476
00:36:18,856 --> 00:36:21,854
So I'm going to look into it myself.

477
00:36:21,879 --> 00:36:26,074
Whether I should give him my blessing,
or put a stop to it.

478
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:28,124
You don't need to look into it.

479
00:36:28,149 --> 00:36:29,982
The owner here is a good guy. Let's go.

480
00:36:30,007 --> 00:36:32,894
Hey. How would you know?

481
00:36:33,916 --> 00:36:37,524
I talked to him a few times,
and I could tell.

482
00:36:38,035 --> 00:36:40,993
Let's go up the street
and have pork belly and soju.

483
00:36:40,994 --> 00:36:43,709
If Gyu Rim finds out we came here,
she'll flip out.

484
00:36:43,837 --> 00:36:48,781
Hey, do you know how a father
with a daughter feels?

485
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:51,903
- No, I don't.
- If you don't, keep your mouth shut.

486
00:36:55,946 --> 00:36:58,487
Heung Sik, let's go.

487
00:37:00,773 --> 00:37:03,500
He is really exhausting.

488
00:37:11,014 --> 00:37:12,200
Welcome.

489
00:37:28,317 --> 00:37:30,846
- You...
- Long time no see.

490
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:35,850
I'm here as a customer to eat
spaghetti today, so lose the glare.

491
00:37:38,620 --> 00:37:41,119
- How many?
- Two.

492
00:37:42,896 --> 00:37:44,114
Mr. Han!

493
00:37:50,207 --> 00:37:51,860
- Who are you?
- Sorry?

494
00:37:53,870 --> 00:37:57,014
Yes. I'm Park Jeong Woo,
manager of Da Solo.

495
00:37:57,134 --> 00:37:59,303
Is Kim Mu Jin the owner
of this restaurant?

496
00:37:59,541 --> 00:38:01,835
I heard he's a co-owner, though.

497
00:38:04,214 --> 00:38:06,134
I wonder how big his stake is.

498
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:07,772
Excuse me, but who are you?

499
00:38:09,621 --> 00:38:11,180
He's Han Gyu Rim's father.

500
00:38:11,334 --> 00:38:12,767
No way.

501
00:38:13,094 --> 00:38:15,127
Looks like you know my Gyu Rim.

502
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:20,939
Then you must know Kim Mu Jin
has been following my daughter around too.

503
00:38:30,980 --> 00:38:34,122
- Emergency. Code red.
- What is it?

504
00:38:34,147 --> 00:38:38,000
Gyu Rim's father is at our restaurant.

505
00:38:38,025 --> 00:38:39,344
Okay.

506
00:38:41,077 --> 00:38:44,739
- What? Who?
- Gyu Rim's father.

507
00:38:45,491 --> 00:38:48,380
- What?
- Get over here.

508
00:38:52,516 --> 00:38:54,013
All of a sudden?

509
00:38:56,674 --> 00:38:59,722
Property values around here are no joke.

510
00:38:59,747 --> 00:39:02,360
Then the deposit and rent
must be expensive too.

511
00:39:03,767 --> 00:39:07,307
If he can afford
a deposit and rent that steep,

512
00:39:07,734 --> 00:39:09,699
he must have plenty of money, right?

513
00:39:09,941 --> 00:39:12,380
Is money really that important?

514
00:39:12,501 --> 00:39:15,540
As long as he can keep
his wife and kids fed.

515
00:39:15,541 --> 00:39:18,241
Hey, who goes hungry these days?

516
00:39:22,342 --> 00:39:24,647
Hey, why is this so expensive?

517
00:39:26,061 --> 00:39:28,290
If he can sell food this expensive,

518
00:39:28,404 --> 00:39:31,274
he must be making good money too, right?

519
00:39:31,526 --> 00:39:34,574
Please, look at the man, not the money.

520
00:39:34,987 --> 00:39:36,620
As long as the man himself is decent,

521
00:39:36,621 --> 00:39:38,354
why keep going on about money?

522
00:39:38,540 --> 00:39:42,522
And didn't I tell you
I'd vouch for Kim Mu Jin?

523
00:39:42,547 --> 00:39:44,174
What are you, Kim Mu Jin's spokesman?

524
00:39:46,692 --> 00:39:48,921
You used to like my Gyu Rim.

525
00:39:49,086 --> 00:39:51,869
I forgot all about that.

526
00:39:52,947 --> 00:39:55,046
I shouldn't have brought you.

527
00:39:55,579 --> 00:39:57,640
You're the only one I know who's free.

528
00:39:57,665 --> 00:40:00,707
Gyu Rim is just a friend now.

529
00:40:00,777 --> 00:40:05,167
I really just want my friend
to meet a good guy and be happy.

530
00:40:06,436 --> 00:40:10,961
I'm a man too, but I look around
and there's nobody like Kim Mu Jin.

531
00:40:10,962 --> 00:40:11,962
Enough.

532
00:40:13,334 --> 00:40:14,472
I don't listen to the enemy.

533
00:40:14,497 --> 00:40:17,278
Now that you're recommending him,
I'm suddenly worried.

534
00:40:17,459 --> 00:40:19,027
This is driving me nuts, honestly.

535
00:40:19,506 --> 00:40:22,337
I say a good guy is good,
and I still get grief for it.

536
00:40:24,494 --> 00:40:26,477
Heung Sik. Hey.

537
00:40:27,169 --> 00:40:30,060
Does Kim Mu Jin have any health problems?

538
00:40:30,614 --> 00:40:31,759
Is he really single?

539
00:40:31,761 --> 00:40:34,281
Is he two-timing some woman?

540
00:40:34,821 --> 00:40:36,520
Or does he have a secret kid?

541
00:40:36,521 --> 00:40:38,274
- No, I don't.
- No?

542
00:40:43,787 --> 00:40:44,918
I've never been married.

543
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:47,587
I've never two-timed anyone,
and I have no secret kids.

544
00:40:47,774 --> 00:40:52,046
And I had a checkup three months ago,
and all the results were normal.

545
00:40:52,334 --> 00:40:54,780
See? He says no.

546
00:40:55,107 --> 00:40:57,840
Why are you so suspicious of people?

547
00:40:59,714 --> 00:41:03,012
I heard you told Gyu Rim
you want to start over?

548
00:41:03,633 --> 00:41:04,633
Yes.

549
00:41:05,985 --> 00:41:07,107
Good call.

550
00:41:07,234 --> 00:41:10,630
You could search the whole world
and never find anyone like Gyu Rim.

551
00:41:11,667 --> 00:41:13,267
Of course. I know.

552
00:41:14,707 --> 00:41:17,700
It's an honor to have you come
all the way to my humble place, sir.

553
00:41:17,741 --> 00:41:21,184
I should've contacted you first and
invited you myself. I'm sorry I didn't.

554
00:41:27,821 --> 00:41:31,400
But why does that cricket-looking guy
keep glaring at me?

555
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:49,988
That's my roommate, and the co-owner here.

556
00:41:50,067 --> 00:41:51,753
He hasn't had a girlfriend in ten years.

557
00:41:51,755 --> 00:41:55,850
But I have a woman I love,
and now you've even come to see me,

558
00:41:55,875 --> 00:41:57,943
so I think he must be a little jealous.

559
00:41:59,193 --> 00:42:02,564
That's a shame. He looks like a nice kid.

560
00:42:02,747 --> 00:42:04,223
If you haven't decided what to order yet,

561
00:42:04,224 --> 00:42:06,267
may I choose the dishes for you myself?

562
00:42:06,507 --> 00:42:09,388
If there's anything
you can't eat or don't like,

563
00:42:09,583 --> 00:42:10,814
please let me know anytime.

564
00:42:11,707 --> 00:42:12,707
- Nothing.
- Nothing.

565
00:42:12,828 --> 00:42:13,828
Okay.

566
00:42:23,094 --> 00:42:24,351
How much does all this cost?

567
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:27,853
Hey, what's your mom's credit limit?

568
00:42:28,751 --> 00:42:29,847
What credit card?

569
00:42:32,747 --> 00:42:37,569
This is the most expensive wine we have.
Shall I open it for you?

570
00:42:37,691 --> 00:42:39,874
We didn't order that.

571
00:42:40,580 --> 00:42:44,104
But if it's on the house,
we'll gladly drink it.

572
00:42:45,907 --> 00:42:48,053
Mu Jin is treating you.

573
00:42:48,345 --> 00:42:50,025
As for all this food here,

574
00:42:50,099 --> 00:42:54,472
our boss, Kim Mu Jin,
is paying for it all with his own card.

575
00:42:54,907 --> 00:42:56,167
Seriously?

576
00:42:56,847 --> 00:42:58,123
Honestly...

577
00:42:58,454 --> 00:43:00,315
"A man should have some shame."

578
00:43:00,490 --> 00:43:02,434
"How can I impose on him like this?"

579
00:43:03,913 --> 00:43:07,387
If you feel that way and insist on paying,

580
00:43:07,412 --> 00:43:09,576
I'll gladly help you
with the bill anytime.

581
00:43:11,187 --> 00:43:14,853
- You said he looked like a nice kid?
- I take it back.

582
00:43:17,901 --> 00:43:20,401
Would you like a taste first?

583
00:43:20,873 --> 00:43:24,940
We'll pour it ourselves,
so you can go now.

584
00:43:25,253 --> 00:43:27,957
Yes. You can go now.

585
00:43:28,841 --> 00:43:31,407
I already hate the crickets
outside my window.

586
00:43:36,013 --> 00:43:38,369
Rude little punk.

587
00:43:38,874 --> 00:43:40,587
Minus ten points because of him.

588
00:43:40,588 --> 00:43:42,255
That's not fair.

589
00:43:42,282 --> 00:43:45,702
By that logic, Gyu Rim loses 100 points
for having you as her father.

590
00:43:47,474 --> 00:43:50,864
How much is this wine?

591
00:43:51,823 --> 00:43:53,874
Chateau Paris.

592
00:43:56,500 --> 00:44:00,380
Looks like Kim Mu Jin blew
his whole paycheck to treat you.

593
00:44:01,673 --> 00:44:06,627
He's generous and bold. The more
I see of him, the more I like him.

594
00:44:07,369 --> 00:44:08,665
Please, try it.

595
00:44:15,294 --> 00:44:16,294
How is it?

596
00:44:19,507 --> 00:44:20,727
It's so good.

597
00:44:20,752 --> 00:44:23,765
This stuff's precious,
so drink just a little.

598
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:25,640
Why? Let's drink it together.

599
00:44:26,090 --> 00:44:27,600
It's too precious.

600
00:44:50,907 --> 00:44:52,194
Top-grade chuck flap.

601
00:45:05,214 --> 00:45:07,618
Now you're even bringing out the caviar?

602
00:45:09,569 --> 00:45:11,052
You're even sprinkling gold on it?

603
00:45:11,346 --> 00:45:15,940
Just give it all away.
Why not give him the whole restaurant?

604
00:45:30,294 --> 00:45:33,657
- Dad.
- My youngest daughter.

605
00:45:34,173 --> 00:45:37,044
- Gyu Min, you work here?
- Yes.

606
00:45:37,947 --> 00:45:39,767
Why did you come here in person?

607
00:45:39,768 --> 00:45:41,955
You only asked me for the name
of Mu Jin's restaurant.

608
00:45:44,514 --> 00:45:46,280
Why did you order so much?

609
00:45:46,634 --> 00:45:48,167
And only the most expensive dishes?

610
00:45:48,427 --> 00:45:51,637
It's fine. It's all free.

611
00:45:53,054 --> 00:45:55,228
- It really is free.
- Sorry?

612
00:45:59,300 --> 00:46:02,081
Did you throw a fit
to get it for free again?

613
00:46:02,214 --> 00:46:03,921
You brat, what do you take me for?

614
00:46:04,660 --> 00:46:07,034
This is all my son-in-law Kim's treat.

615
00:46:07,367 --> 00:46:08,747
Son-in-law Kim?

616
00:46:08,857 --> 00:46:13,041
Yes, son-in-law Kim.
Or my son-in-law, or Kim Mu Jin.

617
00:46:13,387 --> 00:46:18,000
You can just call him your brother-in-law.
It's all settled.

618
00:46:32,406 --> 00:46:33,999
You're really not going in?

619
00:46:37,621 --> 00:46:38,976
Let's just go.

620
00:46:39,067 --> 00:46:41,313
We came all this way,
and we're just leaving?

621
00:46:44,721 --> 00:46:46,871
Go. Forget it.

622
00:46:49,086 --> 00:46:52,500
Mom, it's been eight years already.

623
00:46:52,799 --> 00:46:56,538
If this keeps up,
you and Mu Jin might really be over.

624
00:46:58,036 --> 00:47:00,342
Either get Mu Jin to surrender,

625
00:47:00,662 --> 00:47:03,281
or you surrender to Mu Jin.

626
00:47:03,794 --> 00:47:05,565
Why should I surrender?

627
00:47:06,400 --> 00:47:07,814
I'd sooner die and come back as a ghost...

628
00:47:07,961 --> 00:47:09,761
than accept that Han Gyu Rim.

629
00:47:10,470 --> 00:47:11,820
Go. Start the car.

630
00:47:13,687 --> 00:47:14,687
Mom.

631
00:47:15,417 --> 00:47:18,487
Should I drive? Should I just call a taxi?

632
00:47:37,577 --> 00:47:38,887
My son-in-law.

633
00:47:39,527 --> 00:47:43,127
Hey. As of today,
you're my son-in-law. Got it?

634
00:47:43,287 --> 00:47:44,740
Thank you.

635
00:47:46,339 --> 00:47:49,797
Hey. Tell Gyu Rim right away.

636
00:47:49,821 --> 00:47:52,001
That as of today, he's my son-in-law.

637
00:47:52,181 --> 00:47:54,994
Can't we take it slow?

638
00:47:54,995 --> 00:47:58,458
Things are moving so fast
that I can't keep up.

639
00:47:58,461 --> 00:48:01,855
If you wait here a moment,
I'll get the car ready and drive you home.

640
00:48:02,330 --> 00:48:05,962
What planet are you from?

641
00:48:05,987 --> 00:48:10,567
How did you end up falling from the sky
in front of my daughter?

642
00:48:11,054 --> 00:48:12,214
Did you just parachute in here?

643
00:48:13,747 --> 00:48:15,576
He seems pretty drunk,

644
00:48:15,578 --> 00:48:17,906
so I'll take him home. You can head out.

645
00:48:17,907 --> 00:48:20,653
If you drive him home,
that cricket-looking guy might kill you.

646
00:48:20,655 --> 00:48:21,835
No, it's no trouble.

647
00:48:22,249 --> 00:48:25,869
If his mood gets any better,
he'll try to hug and kiss you.

648
00:48:25,894 --> 00:48:27,351
Can you handle that?

649
00:48:27,976 --> 00:48:29,693
See you next time, sir.

650
00:48:29,718 --> 00:48:31,634
Okay, my son-in-law.

651
00:48:31,659 --> 00:48:33,716
That's enough, Mr. Han.

652
00:48:33,997 --> 00:48:36,214
He has a business to run.

653
00:48:37,261 --> 00:48:38,261
Let's go.

654
00:48:38,262 --> 00:48:39,382
What's this?

655
00:48:39,607 --> 00:48:42,985
Go get her, son-in-law!

656
00:48:43,022 --> 00:48:44,228
You too.

657
00:48:44,781 --> 00:48:47,087
- You got this!
- You got this!

658
00:48:47,524 --> 00:48:49,020
You got this!

659
00:48:49,133 --> 00:48:51,581
- Let's go.
- You got this!

660
00:48:51,607 --> 00:48:54,441
Wipe your drool, at least. Seriously.

661
00:48:57,665 --> 00:49:00,824
I don't know what's going on.

662
00:49:01,327 --> 00:49:03,354
You told me never to call you again...

663
00:49:04,294 --> 00:49:05,674
What brings you here at this hour?

664
00:49:06,861 --> 00:49:08,477
That's why I called you.

665
00:49:11,860 --> 00:49:16,496
I mean, what kind of life have I lived?

666
00:49:16,860 --> 00:49:20,977
Why are you the only friend
I can call when things are hard?

667
00:49:22,300 --> 00:49:25,221
It's humiliating. It ticks me off.

668
00:49:26,634 --> 00:49:27,847
Honestly.

669
00:49:35,307 --> 00:49:39,549
Hey, so when is your wife coming back?

670
00:49:41,373 --> 00:49:44,577
Hey, are you really planning
to get a divorce or something?

671
00:49:47,401 --> 00:49:49,008
Silly me.

672
00:49:49,574 --> 00:49:51,492
I forgot the wine glasses again.

673
00:49:51,517 --> 00:49:53,152
Forget it. I'm leaving.

674
00:49:53,780 --> 00:49:55,440
Leaving? Where? Okay, fine.

675
00:49:55,485 --> 00:49:56,805
Then let's just drink out of these.

676
00:49:57,584 --> 00:49:59,359
You don't answer anything I ask,

677
00:49:59,384 --> 00:50:01,547
you're half out of it,
and you're no fun at all.

678
00:50:01,572 --> 00:50:02,627
I'm going.

679
00:50:04,061 --> 00:50:05,081
Going?

680
00:50:07,003 --> 00:50:08,030
Fun?

681
00:50:08,055 --> 00:50:13,853
Are you going off to meet
that fun sparkling water guy?

682
00:50:14,234 --> 00:50:15,522
What? Sparkling water guy?

683
00:50:15,547 --> 00:50:18,374
You know, that weird guy
we saw at that noodle place.

684
00:50:19,701 --> 00:50:21,156
Weird guy? Hey.

685
00:50:22,341 --> 00:50:23,901
Are you really seeing him?

686
00:50:24,141 --> 00:50:25,667
Get a grip.

687
00:50:26,134 --> 00:50:28,674
He's a really weird guy.
I don't think he's all there.

688
00:50:28,821 --> 00:50:30,234
A guy who suits you...

689
00:50:30,454 --> 00:50:32,651
He doesn't suit you. Not him.

690
00:50:32,901 --> 00:50:36,861
Hey, who are you to badmouth my friend?

691
00:50:36,886 --> 00:50:37,994
Friend?

692
00:50:38,604 --> 00:50:41,067
Yes. He's my friend.

693
00:50:42,140 --> 00:50:45,647
Do you even know what kind of person
he is, talking about him like that?

694
00:50:46,168 --> 00:50:49,327
You met him once. Who are you to judge?

695
00:50:49,352 --> 00:50:50,794
You've fallen hard.

696
00:50:51,441 --> 00:50:53,721
You're completely head over heels.

697
00:50:54,228 --> 00:50:56,247
Hey.

698
00:50:56,272 --> 00:50:57,963
You think you're so great?

699
00:50:58,016 --> 00:51:01,056
Right. If you're so great,

700
00:51:01,084 --> 00:51:04,920
why'd you fall for a woman like Ko Yun Hui
and even marry her?

701
00:51:07,194 --> 00:51:08,670
Watch your mouth.

702
00:51:09,354 --> 00:51:12,207
Don't you remember the advice I gave you
when you were going to remarry?

703
00:51:12,441 --> 00:51:14,696
I said the same thing you just said.

704
00:51:14,721 --> 00:51:16,954
That she seemed strange, so be careful.

705
00:51:17,001 --> 00:51:18,747
That she wasn't right for you.

706
00:51:18,772 --> 00:51:22,055
Hey! Get out.

707
00:51:22,567 --> 00:51:24,107
I don't want to talk to you, so get out.

708
00:51:24,474 --> 00:51:25,501
Hey.

709
00:51:25,988 --> 00:51:28,533
Don't you ever contact me again. Got it?

710
00:51:28,747 --> 00:51:29,747
Jang Hun Tae.

711
00:51:29,880 --> 00:51:31,500
Delete my number.

712
00:51:31,768 --> 00:51:32,968
Delete it right now, in front of me.

713
00:51:33,274 --> 00:51:35,760
What, you think I won't delete it?

714
00:51:35,785 --> 00:51:37,175
- Delete it.
- I'm deleting it.

715
00:51:37,468 --> 00:51:40,437
- Don't ever contact me again.
- I'll delete it.

716
00:52:06,907 --> 00:52:08,747
Is this really all you want?

717
00:52:08,806 --> 00:52:11,201
And you even gave me pretty flowers.

718
00:52:11,226 --> 00:52:13,895
Not at all.
Spicy rice cakes are my favorite.

719
00:52:15,714 --> 00:52:17,982
Next time, I'll buy you meat.

720
00:52:18,047 --> 00:52:22,357
I work part-time at a barbecue place now,
and the meat there is really good.

721
00:52:23,027 --> 00:52:25,301
Okay. Please buy me meat next time.

722
00:52:29,105 --> 00:52:32,602
Excuse me, is this yours?

723
00:52:32,692 --> 00:52:36,792
I was looking everywhere for that.
Thank you.

724
00:52:40,026 --> 00:52:42,672
Have some spicy rice cakes.

725
00:52:44,798 --> 00:52:46,170
Thank you.

726
00:52:46,195 --> 00:52:47,394
And water.

727
00:52:48,967 --> 00:52:50,374
Go ahead and eat.

728
00:52:53,641 --> 00:52:55,039
Thank you. This looks great.

729
00:53:06,558 --> 00:53:09,292
I'm sorry.

730
00:53:10,740 --> 00:53:12,681
I was staring too much, wasn't I?

731
00:53:13,407 --> 00:53:14,454
Not at all.

732
00:53:17,860 --> 00:53:22,694
I was just thinking your parents
must be so proud of you.

733
00:53:27,548 --> 00:53:30,414
I don't know about my dad.
I've never asked him.

734
00:53:30,581 --> 00:53:33,247
And my mom wouldn't care.

735
00:53:36,714 --> 00:53:39,230
She left home before I was even three.

736
00:53:39,661 --> 00:53:41,322
She ran off with some man.

737
00:53:44,320 --> 00:53:46,367
So I don't even know what she looks like.

738
00:53:50,617 --> 00:53:52,572
I'm sorry.

739
00:53:52,967 --> 00:53:55,262
I shouldn't have brought it up.

740
00:53:55,986 --> 00:53:57,254
It's okay.

741
00:54:07,968 --> 00:54:09,194
Are you all right?

742
00:54:14,348 --> 00:54:18,529
Slowly. Breathe. Are you okay?

743
00:54:20,168 --> 00:54:22,851
My goodness, I'm sorry.

744
00:54:24,907 --> 00:54:26,624
Drink some water.

745
00:54:35,151 --> 00:54:38,042
(Dad)

746
00:54:38,800 --> 00:54:42,554
You can't let Kim Mu Jin get away.

747
00:54:42,761 --> 00:54:46,124
He is the real deal.

748
00:54:46,168 --> 00:54:48,220
I checked everything out today,

749
00:54:48,327 --> 00:54:51,761
so don't push him away
by going on about knowing your place.

750
00:54:51,841 --> 00:54:53,921
Don't run away. Just grab him.

751
00:54:53,946 --> 00:54:57,961
Stick to him like a fly on flypaper,
no matter what.

752
00:54:57,986 --> 00:55:00,533
Dad, a customer just came in.
I have to go.

753
00:55:04,354 --> 00:55:05,488
Here, eat this.

754
00:55:05,668 --> 00:55:08,168
My mom was craving sweet pancakes,

755
00:55:08,287 --> 00:55:11,181
and she told me to bring you one
since you'd still be at the shop.

756
00:55:11,254 --> 00:55:13,174
Thanks, Heung Sik. I'll enjoy it.

757
00:55:16,240 --> 00:55:20,581
Your dad is totally sold on Kim Mu Jin.

758
00:55:21,324 --> 00:55:25,588
He asked me to come along, so I went
with him to Kim Mu Jin's restaurant,

759
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:30,813
and honestly,
he's a much better guy than I thought.

760
00:55:31,875 --> 00:55:36,824
It sounds like he
wants to start over with you,

761
00:55:36,864 --> 00:55:40,371
so stop running and say yes, okay?

762
00:55:40,401 --> 00:55:44,054
If you let him go,
you'll never meet anyone like him again.

763
00:55:44,487 --> 00:55:46,063
Not you too, Heung Sik.

764
00:55:47,287 --> 00:55:48,927
He and I can't be together.

765
00:55:49,041 --> 00:55:50,914
Never. No way, Heung Sik.

766
00:55:50,939 --> 00:55:54,101
Nothing's impossible, okay?

767
00:55:54,480 --> 00:55:57,493
They say love can cross any border.

768
00:55:57,540 --> 00:55:59,588
I'd sooner cross a border.

769
00:56:00,141 --> 00:56:01,874
But he and I can't be together.

770
00:56:02,433 --> 00:56:03,921
Absolutely not, Heung Sik.

771
00:56:04,461 --> 00:56:08,361
What, is he the only son
of some conglomerate family or something?

772
00:56:08,440 --> 00:56:12,091
If he were, I'd stop you no matter what.

773
00:56:12,137 --> 00:56:15,865
I can already see you suffering
if you marry into a family like that,

774
00:56:15,917 --> 00:56:18,976
so I'd go out of my way to stop you.

775
00:56:22,941 --> 00:56:25,999
He is the only son
of a conglomerate family.

776
00:56:27,361 --> 00:56:28,541
He just has one older sister.

777
00:56:28,608 --> 00:56:32,301
Come on, lady. Quit joking around.

778
00:56:35,434 --> 00:56:39,549
I'm telling you, he's the only son
of a conglomerate family. Kim Mu Jin.

779
00:56:43,634 --> 00:56:45,008
Seriously?

780
00:56:48,924 --> 00:56:53,110
Because of me,
he threw away everything he had,

781
00:56:54,690 --> 00:56:57,654
turned his back on his family,
and left home.

782
00:56:59,847 --> 00:57:03,470
I'm not going back to him.

783
00:57:07,274 --> 00:57:09,259
I'll make him give up somehow.

784
00:57:12,094 --> 00:57:15,626
So that he gets sick of me,
loses all interest,

785
00:57:17,776 --> 00:57:21,236
and runs for his life
without looking back.

786
00:57:22,874 --> 00:57:24,697
I'll make sure of it.

787
00:57:53,547 --> 00:57:54,561
What's this?

788
00:57:55,447 --> 00:57:56,494
What?

789
00:57:57,541 --> 00:57:59,521
I thought you said you'd never
even look our way again.

790
00:58:00,028 --> 00:58:01,648
Aren't there any cold noodle places
near your house?

791
00:58:01,680 --> 00:58:03,223
No. So what?

792
00:58:05,167 --> 00:58:06,388
Something's wrong, isn't it?

793
00:58:06,694 --> 00:58:09,112
If it's not working,
quitting fast is an option too.

794
00:58:09,194 --> 00:58:12,094
Patience was never your thing anyway.

795
00:58:12,188 --> 00:58:14,936
Quit what?
Do you know how happy I am right now?

796
00:58:14,961 --> 00:58:17,777
I got diamond earrings
from my mother-in-law again today.

797
00:58:17,920 --> 00:58:19,949
Then go chew on your diamond earrings.

798
00:58:19,974 --> 00:58:22,158
Why come all the way
to our neighborhood for cold noodles?

799
00:58:23,541 --> 00:58:26,336
Just you try telling dad
and Han Gyu Rim I'm here.

800
00:58:26,361 --> 00:58:29,795
Don't worry. Our family doesn't even
bring you up. It kills our appetite.

801
00:58:29,820 --> 00:58:31,013
What, you little...?

802
00:58:31,334 --> 00:58:33,921
I've stayed long enough. I'm going.

803
00:58:33,946 --> 00:58:34,959
Wait.

804
00:58:38,467 --> 00:58:40,341
Check your messages. I sent you a photo.

805
00:58:44,933 --> 00:58:47,896
- What is this?
- My mother-in-law.

806
00:58:48,154 --> 00:58:50,063
Why would you send me a picture
of your mother-in-law?

807
00:58:53,620 --> 00:58:55,664
So you can memorize her face
and avoid her.

808
00:58:56,279 --> 00:58:57,303
What?

809
00:58:57,708 --> 00:59:02,457
She might end up as one of your clients,
so be smart and steer clear.

810
00:59:02,902 --> 00:59:04,900
If she happens to get hooked on you,

811
00:59:05,153 --> 00:59:07,693
our family tree will get
seriously messed up. Got it?

812
00:59:12,034 --> 00:59:13,997
- Hey!
- If you were a decent person,

813
00:59:15,070 --> 00:59:19,059
if you were really my sister,
you'd tell me to quit that stuff.

814
00:59:19,174 --> 00:59:21,150
You'd tell me to quit that crazy stuff,

815
00:59:21,321 --> 00:59:23,773
and work hard and honestly. You rotten...

816
00:59:28,686 --> 00:59:32,064
If you ever see me on the street,
you'd better avoid me.

817
00:59:32,853 --> 00:59:35,384
Because if I see you again,
I don't know what I'll do.

818
00:59:48,667 --> 00:59:50,953
It's hot. Why is it so hot?

819
00:59:51,508 --> 00:59:54,448
Excuse me, could you turn on the AC?

820
01:00:09,713 --> 01:00:11,790
Gyu O?

821
01:00:17,837 --> 01:00:19,147
Han Gyu O.

822
01:00:22,011 --> 01:00:23,454
Hey, Gyu Rim.

823
01:00:25,477 --> 01:00:27,876
What are you thinking so hard about?

824
01:00:29,287 --> 01:00:30,821
Nothing, just...

825
01:00:32,587 --> 01:00:36,520
"What's in that bag she's carrying?"
That kind of thing.

826
01:00:37,420 --> 01:00:40,911
This? Sweet pancakes.
Heung Sik gave them to me.

827
01:00:41,980 --> 01:00:46,003
- Gyu Seo's crazy about sweet pancakes.
- I know.

828
01:00:46,628 --> 01:00:49,684
Share them nicely with Gyu Seo.
No fighting.

829
01:00:50,207 --> 01:00:53,259
Okay. No fighting, share nicely.

830
01:00:54,367 --> 01:00:58,533
- Let's go.
- You dumped Kim Mu Jin again today?

831
01:01:00,734 --> 01:01:04,014
Why do you keep kicking him so hard?
Are you Son Heung Min?

832
01:01:06,861 --> 01:01:08,526
Who said anything?

833
01:01:11,841 --> 01:01:15,259
Mu Jin and I agreed to be like brothers.

834
01:01:17,547 --> 01:01:18,934
You met Mu Jin?

835
01:01:20,460 --> 01:01:23,927
Even you met Mu Jin?

836
01:01:24,494 --> 01:01:27,243
Stop dumping my brother like that, okay?

837
01:01:27,268 --> 01:01:30,121
You've got strong legs,
so getting kicked by you really hurts.

838
01:01:31,913 --> 01:01:34,109
If you want to kick someone,
kick me instead.

839
01:01:34,974 --> 01:01:37,425
Got it, Gyu Rim? Do this for me.

840
01:01:38,147 --> 01:01:39,498
I'm counting on you.

841
01:01:49,027 --> 01:01:51,901
So stop putting up walls
and stop running away.

842
01:01:52,272 --> 01:01:54,681
To bring you and Mu Jin back together,

843
01:01:54,706 --> 01:01:57,191
I think fate picked me
to be the bridge between you.

844
01:01:57,374 --> 01:02:00,415
A man my mom and I both like a lot.

845
01:02:00,581 --> 01:02:04,160
He is the real deal.

846
01:02:04,532 --> 01:02:06,727
Stop dumping my brother like that.

847
01:02:43,481 --> 01:02:44,487
What?

848
01:02:49,549 --> 01:02:53,040
- What?
- Go outside.

849
01:02:54,294 --> 01:02:55,849
Why? What is it?

850
01:02:55,874 --> 01:02:59,994
I think Gyu Rim has lost her mind.

851
01:03:00,427 --> 01:03:01,966
What are you talking about?

852
01:03:04,174 --> 01:03:07,102
You know how much you hate tigers
and how scared of them you are.

853
01:03:07,194 --> 01:03:08,207
What?

854
01:03:30,093 --> 01:03:31,651
Where is Gyu Rim?

855
01:03:39,403 --> 01:03:40,806
Mu Jin.

856
01:04:07,695 --> 01:04:09,220
It's me, Gyu Rim.

857
01:04:50,063 --> 01:04:51,930
(Love on the Menu)

858
01:04:52,081 --> 01:04:54,574
Gyu Rim is acting weird. Really weird.

859
01:04:54,599 --> 01:04:55,681
This is the real me.

860
01:04:55,814 --> 01:04:57,467
I'm a nutcase who makes
Han Gyu Yeong look tame.

861
01:04:57,492 --> 01:04:58,681
I'm not getting a divorce.

862
01:04:58,706 --> 01:04:59,706
Gyu Yeong.

863
01:04:59,731 --> 01:05:02,412
Let's not get divorced,
and just date other people on our own.

864
01:05:02,437 --> 01:05:03,714
What is she even saying right now?

865
01:05:03,741 --> 01:05:05,361
I didn't know anything for eight years.

866
01:05:05,727 --> 01:05:07,321
I didn't know a thing.

867
01:05:07,394 --> 01:05:10,835
Mom, is your goal to get
rejected by Mu Jin?

868
01:05:10,860 --> 01:05:13,200
If I were you, I'd be so turned off
I'd never want to see her again.

869
01:05:13,225 --> 01:05:14,254
It's kind of annoying.

870
01:05:14,368 --> 01:05:15,607
She just seemed cute and pretty.

871
01:05:15,632 --> 01:05:17,394
This is really bad.

872
01:05:19,002 --> 01:05:20,802
Dramaday.me
